DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
SUMMARY:▲ Long easy run 10 km\, HR under 158. Aerobic base…
DESCRIPTION:Long easy run 10 km\, HR under 158. Aerobic base is the lever
  - the fastest runners get there on Zone 1 volume. LONG RUN WITH A THRES
 HOLD FINISH: last 10 min at threshold EFFORT - HR 175-180\, pace 5:25-5:
 35/km. Only 10 min this week: with Tuesday's 4 x 1 km it puts quality at
  about 23% of the week\, inside the 20-25% cap.\n\nWeek 2 of 11 - Re-ent
 ry\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nRE-ENTRY. 5 KM RETES
 T Tuesday - it sets every pace below. Nothing else hard.\n146 days to Ve
 nice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w3-s0-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Strength UPPER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength UPPER - push and pull as one session\, 45 min. Rows\
 , pull-ups\, overhead press\, rear delts. Heavy\, 4-6 reps\, not hypertr
 ophy ranges. Free against the running and cycling load. Dead hangs 3 x m
 ax at the end - grip is a genuine weakness at 32-36 s.\n\nWeek 3 of 11 -
  Threshold\nTHRESHOLD BLOCK opens. Pfitzinger's order: threshold first\,
  VO2max later in the block. Two quality touches this week - Tuesday's se
 ssion and a threshold finish on the long run. Quality volume stays insid
 e 20-25% of weekly mileage\, which is the Norwegian rule and the one tha
 t keeps this repeatable.\n145 days to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w3-s1-strides@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:THRESHOLD 4 x 1 km at threshold EFFORT (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:THRESHOLD 4 x 1 km at threshold EFFORT - HR 175-180\, pace 5:
 25-5:35/km. This is triangulated\, not guessed: your 1 Sep 4 x 4 min ran
  5:27/5:12/5:20/5:23 at HR 175-178\, and VDOT off the time trial indepen
 dently lands on 5:30. Re-anchor after each retest\, 90 s jog. First qual
 ity session of the block - deliberately conservative. Warm up 15 min + 4
  x 100 m AT 5:15/km and no faster\, cool down 10 min.\n\nWeek 3 of 11 - 
 Threshold\nTHRESHOLD BLOCK opens. Pfitzinger's order: threshold first\, 
 VO2max later in the block. Two quality touches this week - Tuesday's ses
 sion and a threshold finish on the long run. Quality volume stays inside
  20-25% of weekly mileage\, which is the Norwegian rule and the one that
  keeps this repeatable.\n144 days to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
