BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w4-s0-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Strength UPPER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength UPPER - push and pull as one session\, 45 min. Rows\
 , pull-ups\, overhead press\, rear delts. Heavy\, 4-6 reps\, not hypertr
 ophy ranges. Free against the running and cycling load. Dead hangs 3 x m
 ax at the end - grip is a genuine weakness at 32-36 s.\n\nWeek 4 of 11 -
  Threshold\nTHRESHOLD. Sub-threshold means controlled\, not max. If you 
 cannot finish the last rep at the same pace as the first\, you ran the f
 irst too fast.\n138 days to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w4-s1-strides@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:THRESHOLD 4 x 1.5 km at threshold EFFORT (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:THRESHOLD 4 x 1.5 km at threshold EFFORT - HR 175-180\, pace 
 5:25-5:35/km. This is triangulated\, not guessed: your 1 Sep 4 x 4 min r
 an 5:27/5:12/5:20/5:23 at HR 175-178\, and VDOT off the time trial indep
 endently lands on 5:30. Re-anchor after each retest\, 90 s jog. Controll
 ed\, not max. Ceiling as well as target: if HR drifts past 183 on the la
 st two\, you started too fast. Warm up 15 min\, cool down 10 min.\n\nWee
 k 4 of 11 - Threshold\nTHRESHOLD. Sub-threshold means controlled\, not m
 ax. If you cannot finish the last rep at the same pace as the first\, yo
 u ran the first too fast.\n137 days to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w4-s2-swim@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261210
SUMMARY:≈ Swim 07:00 Sloterparkbad (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Swim 07:00 Sloterparkbad - technique\, self-coached (coach la
 ter)\, 45 min. Warm-up 100 m + 10 bobs\; 15 min of drills (side kick\, 6
 -1-6\, catch-up\, one-arm\, fingertip drag - whichever still feels harde
 st)\; then this week's continuous-swim set from the Sunday swim\, easy. 
 Cool-down 100 m. 50 m pool\, lanes 07:00-08:00\, before work.\n\nWeek 4 
 of 11 - Threshold\nTHRESHOLD. Sub-threshold means controlled\, not max. 
 If you cannot finish the last rep at the same pace as the first\, you ra
 n the first too fast.\n136 days to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w4-s3-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261210
SUMMARY:○ BIKE 40 min
DESCRIPTION:BIKE 40 min - sweet spot\, 3 x 8 min at 88-93% FTP (~132-140 
 W)\, 3 min easy between\, the rest as warm-up and cool-down. The 90 km b
 ike is over half a 70.3 by time.\n\nWeek 4 of 11 - Threshold\nTHRESHOLD.
  Sub-threshold means controlled\, not max. If you cannot finish the last
  rep at the same pace as the first\, you ran the first too fast.\n136 da
 ys to Venice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:venice703winterbase-w4-s4-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20261115T161414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:◆ Strength LOWER (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength LOWER - HEAVY\, 45 min. Back squat 4 x 3-5 at 85-90%
  1RM\, safety pins on (75 x 5 on 13 Nov puts the 1RM near 88-90 kg: 4 x 
 4 at 80 kg on 20 Nov\, then add 2.5 kg when the last set moves well). Ha
 ck squat if there's no rack or you're wrecked. Then Bulgarian split squa
 t 3 x 5/leg heavy\, single-leg calf raises 3 x 8 loaded\, Nordic curls 2
  x 4. COMPLEX PAIRING: after each heavy set\, 5 box jumps or 20 m of bou
 nds within 2 min - heavy resistance plus plyo beats either alone for run
 ning economy. Heavy loads at or above 90% 1RM give greater economy gains
  than lighter ones\, and the effect needs 10-14 weeks\, which is exactly
  this block. LOWER-LEG AND FOOT\, 5 min: tibialis anterior raises 3 x 15
 -20\, heel walks 2 x 20 m\, eccentric dorsiflexion 3 x 10\, short-foot h
 olds 3 x 30 s per side.\n\nWeek 4 of 11 - Threshold\nTHRESHOLD. Sub-thre
 shold means controlled\, not max. If you cannot finish the last rep at t
 he same pace as the first\, you ran the first too fast.\n135 days to Ven
 ice 70.3 (winter base).
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
